%U A303380 21114,1531,471,1125,76,77,18,9,13145,21174,5131,1135,1521,167,177,78,19,10
%N A303380 A(n, k) is the smallest number x > A(n, k-1) such that every letter, with repetition, that occurs in the English name of A(n, k-1) also occurs in the English name of x, with A(n, 1) = n; square array, read by antidiagonals downwards.
%C A303380 If A(n,k) = A(m,j), then A(n,k+i) = A(m,j+i) for i >= 0. Thus A(1,k) = A(3,k-1) for k >= 7. - _Robert Israel_, Aug 11 2026
%H A303380 Robert Israel, <a href="/A303380/b303380.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..630</a> (first 35 antidiagonals, flattened)
%H A303380 <a href="/index/Na">Index entries for sequences related to names of numbers</a>
%F A303380 A(n, 1) = n. For k > 1, A(n, k) = A303475(A(n, k-1)).
